# Dustfile — rollback, recovery and deprecation for sim-insolvency.
# Verb:      dust
# Authority: advisory
#
# Declaration only — see ../INDEX.a2ml on shape.

@abstract:
How to undo things here, and what has been retired. Most of this repository is
recoverable by rebuild: the only irreplaceable artefacts are authored scenario
content and the decision record.
@end

## Recovery

### rebuild-from-source
- description: Every binary artefact is reproducible from source.
- procedure: "just clean && just build && just test"
- irrecoverable: "nothing — zig-out/, .zig-cache/ and dist/ are all derived"

### rebuild-learner-bundle
- description: dist/ is gitignored and derived.
- procedure: "just standalone (or `just hidden-truth`, which packages one if absent)"
- notes: tools/package-standalone.sh REFUSES if the destination exists. Move the old bundle aside rather than forcing — the refusal is a guard against a half-overwritten bundle being scanned as if fresh.

### recover-certificate-verification
- description: A certificate can be re-verified without the original run.
- procedure: "just verify-certificate <file> <key> — recomputes the digest and signature from the envelope's own fields"
- notes: Requires the key it was signed with. Development-key certificates verify with the published development key by design.

## Irreplaceable

### authored-scenario-content
- description: scenarios/morrow-engineering-001/ is hand-authored, including the hidden reality that the whole assessment depends on.
- backup: "git history only"
- notes: There is exactly one scenario. Losing it loses the product.

### decision-record
- description: docs/architecture/adr/ and the programme registers under programme/.
- backup: "git history only"

## Deprecated / retired

### bespoke-machine-readable-state
- what: ".machine_readable/STATE.a2ml (a bespoke [project]/[claims] pair)"
- retired: "2026-08-07"
- replaced_by: ".machine_readable/descriptiles/STATE.a2ml"
- notes: The original [claims] block is preserved verbatim in the replacement so no claim was silently dropped.

### empty-scaffold-directories
- what: "tests/, benches/, fixtures/, certificates/ — directory trees containing no files"
- retired: "2026-08-04 (tests/), 2026-08-07 (remainder)"
- rationale: "Empty scaffolding implies a suite that does not exist. Zig tests are inline in zig/src/ and run via `zig build test`; the real fixtures live under scenarios/*/fixtures/."

### seven-canary-hidden-truth-suite
- what: "the 7-canary form of tools/test-hidden-truth-scanner.sh"
- retired: "2026-08-04"
- replaced_by: "9 canaries — a drift-channel canary and a runtime positive-marker canary were added after review found the runtime channel could pass vacuously"
- notes: Retained here because the number appears in older documents and pull-request bodies.
